# Code Quality

- Inspect surrounding code and repository conventions before editing.
- Keep changes scoped to the request and preserve unrelated user changes.
- Never hardcode credentials, tokens, private keys, or environment-specific secrets.
- Validate inputs at trust boundaries and handle failure paths explicitly.
- Prefer simple, maintainable designs with clear ownership over speculative abstractions.
- Run the narrowest relevant build, lint, typecheck, and tests after changes.
- Use the `code-review` skill before declaring changed code complete.
